#PDF Processing

from PyPDF2 import PdfReader

def extract_pdf_text(file_path):
    reader = PdfReader(file_path)

    text = ""
    #Read every page
    for page in reader.pages:
        content = page.extract_text() #Extract text from every page
        if content: #If content exists
            text += content + "\n" #Add it to text and in case of a new page move to a new line

    return text

#Integration with Gemini Model

from google import genai
#Integrate and fetch from gemini API
client = genai.Client(api_key="YOUR_API_KEY")
#Use prompt eng
def generate_notes(text):
    prompt = f"""
    Convert this content into structured
    NEET revision notes.

    Include:
    1. Important concepts
    2. Key definitions
    3. Important points

    Content:
    {text}
    """
    #From models.generate_content choose the model and provide the prompt as content
    response = client.models.generate_content(
        model="YOUR_AVAILABLE_GEMINI_MODEL",
        contents=prompt
    )

    return response.text
• LLM (Large Language Model): It is an AI program trained on massive amounts of text so it can understand, summarize, and write like a human.
• Prompt engineering: It is the skill of writing clear, specific instructions to get the best and most accurate answers from an AI.
• Gemini API: It is a bridge that lets developers connect Google's Gemini AI directly into their own apps, websites, or code.
• PDF text extraction: It is the process of using code to automatically copy and pull the readable words out of a digital PDF file.
• If a PDF is scanned: The computer sees the pages as flat pictures rather than selectable text, so standard text-copying tools will return nothing.
• OCR (Optical Character Recognition): It is technology that "reads" pictures of text (like a scanned document or photo) and turns them into real, editable words.
• Tokenization: It is how an AI chops up sentences into small pieces—like whole words or parts of words—so it can count and process them.
• Hallucination: It is when an AI confidently makes up false facts or details because it is guessing the next word rather than knowing the truth.
• Handling a very large PDF: You break the big document into smaller chunks, summarize each piece separately, and then combine those mini-summaries into one final overview.
• Improving summary accuracy: You give the AI strict rules to only use facts from the provided text, ask it to cite page numbers, and request bullet points instead of long paragraphs.

